  "generated_description": "<div class=\"mountain-description prose prose-stone max-w-none\">\n  <p><strong>Vernal Fall</strong> rises to 5,900 feet in California. The Mist Trail to Vernal Fall covers 5.4 miles round trip (out-and-back) with about 1,000 feet of elevation gain \u2014 a gradual walk with modest climbing.</p>\n  <h3>The Route</h3><p>Most of the climbing comes early \u2014 the first half of the route does the bulk of the work before the grade eases. The steepest stretch arrives around mile 0.23, gaining roughly 2,600 feet per mile \u2014 expect a slow, deliberate pace through here. From the trailhead at about 4,000 feet, the route tops out near 5,000 feet. Along the way the route passes a boulder (Lady Franklin Rock) near mile 0.71, a waterfall (Vernal Fall) near mile 0.81, a viewpoint (Clark Point) near mile 0.81 \u2014 useful checkpoints for judging your pace.</p>\n  <h3>Getting There</h3><p>The trailhead is at <a href=\"https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&destination=37.73282,-119.55778\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">37.73282, -119.55778</a> (tap for driving directions). It's roughly 125 miles south of Reno, Nevada. Parking: Happy Isles or Curry Village. Fee: $35 vehicle entrance fee.</p>\n  <h3>When to Go</h3><p>Late May through October is the main season. Snow and ice linger into spring and return early in fall at this latitude and elevation; in winter this becomes a different, more serious undertaking requiring traction devices and warm layers.</p>\n  <h3>Know Before You Go</h3><p>The Moderate rating comes from the National Park Service difficulty formula, which weighs total distance against elevation gain. Most hikers should budget about 4 hours of moving time; add margin for breaks, photos and the descent. Download the GPX track from this page before you go \u2014 cell coverage is unreliable in the mountains and a saved route works offline in any GPS app. Conditions change: verify current access, closures and weather with the official land manager before you go. Trail data is sourced from National Park Service - Yosemite.</p>\n  <p>Looking to link objectives or plan a weekend? Nearby summits include Nevada Fall, Half Dome and Upper Yosemite Fall \u2014 each has its own guide on this site.</p>\n</div>",
